"[2511.07568v1] Procedural Knowledge Improves Agentic LLM Workflows (https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.07568v1)\nciteturn1996view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.07568v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 159\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Artificial Intelligence\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 10 Nov 2025]\nL9: # Title:Procedural Knowledge Improves Agentic LLM Workflows\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Vincent Hsiao , cite6†Mark Roberts , cite7†Leslie Smith L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Procedural Knowledge Improves Agentic LLM Workflows, by Vincent Hsiao and 2 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite8†View PDF cite9†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Large language models (LLMs) often struggle when performing agentic tasks without substantial tool support, prom-pt engineering, or fine tuning. Despite research showing that domain-dependent, procedural knowledge can dramatically increase planning efficiency, little work evaluates its potential for improving LLM performance on agentic tasks that may require implicit planning.\nL17: We formalize, implement, and evaluate an agentic LLM workflow that leverages procedural knowledge in the form of a hierarchical task network (HTN). Empirical results of our implementation show that hand-coded HTNs can dramatically improve LLM performance on agentic tasks, and using HTNs can boost a 20b or 70b parameter LLM to outperform a much larger 120b parameter LLM baseline. Furthermore, LLM-created HTNs improve overall performance, though less so.\nL18: The results suggest that leveraging expertise--from humans, documents, or LLMs--to curate procedural knowledge will become another important tool for improving LLM workflows.\nL19: Subjects:  | Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI)\nL20: Cite as:  | cite10†arXiv:2511.07568 [cs.AI]\nL21:    | (or cite11†arXiv:2511.07568v1 [cs.AI] for this version)\nL22:    | cite12†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2511.07568†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: ## Submission history\nL24: \nL25: From: Vincent Hsiao [cite13†view email ]\nL26: [v1] Mon, 10 Nov 2025 19:27:57 UTC (1,817 KB)\nL27: \nL28: Full-text links:\nL29: \nL30: ## Access Paper:\nL31: \nL32: View a PDF of the paper titled Procedural Knowledge Improves Agentic LLM Workflows, by Vincent Hsiao and 2 other authors\nL33: \nL34:   * cite8†View PDF L35:   * cite9†HTML (experimental) L36:   * cite14†TeX Source L37: \nL38: cite15†view license L39: \nL40: ### Current browse context:\nL41: \nL42: cs.AI\nL43: \nL44: cite16†< prev |   cite17†next > L45: \nL46: cite18†new | cite19†recent | cite20†2025-11 L47: \nL48: Change to browse by:\nL49: \nL50: cite21†cs L51: ### References & Citations\nL52: \nL53:   * cite22†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L54:   * cite23†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L55:   * cite24†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L56: \nL57: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL58: \nL59: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL60: \nL61: [Button: ×]\nL62: \nL63: loading...\nL64: \nL65: Data provided by:\nL66: \nL67: ### Bookmark\nL68: \nL69: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL70: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL71: \nL72: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL73: \nL74: Bibliographic Explorer (cite25†What is the Explorer?†info.arxiv.org )\nL75: \nL76: [Input] Connected Papers Toggle\nL77: \nL78: Connected Papers (cite26†What is Connected Papers?†www.connectedpapers.com )\nL79: \nL80: [Input] Litmaps Toggle\nL81: \nL82: Litmaps (cite27†What is Litmaps?†www.litmaps.co )\nL83: \nL84: [Input] scite.ai Toggle\nL85: \nL86: scite Smart Citations (cite28†What are Smart Citations?†www.scite.ai )\nL87: \nL88: [Inp